t(11, 215, """In closing: I have seen only two points of the document, and on their basis I wrote this reply. In closing, this document will not succeed, because the burden is far heavier than a mere document! The global burden. The world carries on its bent back a very heavy load, and no document whatsoever can bring this load down from the world's back! The matter is far bigger than a document! Trump knows that, the world's politicians know that, and the palaces of power in Europe, in the islands of the Eastern alliance and in Moscow understand all this. The load the world carries on its shoulder is a load made by many parties, allied and opposed, over 80 years, made with care and precision, and the document is nothing but an organized yet exposed media operation; it is no more than deliberate, intentional propaganda, but very naive and very exposed, and this document can never be bought in the world's palaces of power. It is only marketed to the people, and the news channels market it in order to mislead. It is a misleading document par excellence, for the United States will never give up Europe or the islands of the Eastern alliance, because the issue is not, as it is promoted, that the merchant is angry and the merchant wants bundles of dollars! That is what they want the world to see, and they have indeed managed to make the world see it. But which world? It is the world of the common people, not the world of the world's politicians and the makers of strategies!""")

t(11, 1915, """Studied, disciplined public work by women is a sign that the Ummah has matured in its understanding of the Book of its Mighty Lord and the Sunnah of its Prophet ﷺ""")

t(12, 1555, """The news will be very plentiful and daily, and Allah knows best, according to what is understood from the texts of weak chain and from the general visions""")

t(13, 200, """It came in one of Nu'aym ibn Hammad's weak narrations: he enters Bayt al-Maqdis between seventeen thousand fighters lined up along the road to Jerusalem, with his head bowed""")

t(13, 1380, """In the society of the virtuous city .. simple jobs are a privilege for those who hold them, because their work does not cost them exhausting mental effort, while the kind and quality of personal life they obtain is equal to that of others! And this is the difference between the virtuous city and any other!""")

t(14, 1065, """The media plays a prominent role in informing society of its rights and duties, and in conveying governmental information, whether social, economic or political, widely and comprehensively, so that no one in society is ignorant of any social variable and the pace of change in society becomes slow or lame!""")

t(14, 2265, """The ministry chair is merely a symbol .. a symbol for keeping the work in order .. because every work must have a leader .. but it is not necessarily the chair through which the work is run .. Field work will remain far from leaning on a desk and clinging to a desk chair; field work will remain the best method of high achievement""")

t(15, 905, """Righteousness and piety always shelter under the tree of loyalty to Allah the Exalted!
Loyalty is the greatest motive for piety and commitment, while lack of loyalty to Allah the Exalted is the greatest motive for loyalty to the accursed Iblis. The question has long been one that closes only with the death of each of us, and its recurring text is: how do we become pious?

If you give your loyalty to Allah the Exalted, you will feel that His religion and what He commanded are your responsibility, which you carry with all strength in your hands and on your shoulders, and then sins, except the smallest of the small that is not repeated, sins will be your enemy! What is right will not be your enemy, as is the case with many, though not all! Many, when told to fear Allah, turn hostile to piety and regard it as their enemy, and the reason is that they have not given their loyalty to Allah. How can you be loyal to someone and then work against him? And to Allah the Exalted belongs the highest example: if you are loyal to your father, will you conspire against him? If you are loyal to your mother, will you conspire against her? If you are loyal to your ruler, will you conspire against him? If you are loyal to your manager, will you conspire against him?

To Allah belongs the highest example: loyalty to Allah the Exalted means that you do not conspire against His commands! If a person conspires against Allah's commands, rejects them, repels them, hates them and detests them, is he loyal to Allah the Exalted?

On the other hand, what does it mean that you are loyal to Allah the Exalted? It means that you are angry for His sake. So how are we angry for Allah the Mighty, when He is one Lord and God, the One and Only, who does not need His servants to be angry for Him? We are angry for Allah when we are angry at our own souls' rejection of what is right! When our souls reject what is right, they declare defiance of Allah the Exalted, declare that they do not love Allah the Exalted, and declare that they do not care about Allah the Exalted. So are these acts of the soul toward Allah the Exalted met by you with approval and applause for this soul, or with anger at it? If you applaud it, then it is the one you are loyal to; if you are angry at it and restrain it, then you are loyal to Allah.

The issue, then, in the matter of piety and commitment, is that it needs a thought built on a method, not a sermon titled: O people, fear Allah .. O people, seek forgiveness .. O people, do not disobey Allah .. Oh my! How easy this talk is! Fine, how do we fear Allah? Or are these just parrot phrases, with no guidance for people regarding the method through which their minds understand the entrance and the door to the fear of Allah?

So as long as you are not loyal to Allah, never dream of fearing Allah .. you will keep going around in a vicious circle .. because you do not regard Allah the Exalted as a God for whom one gets angry. And anger for Him is not that you go and impose religion on society; that is not your role, that is a matter within the ruler's competence. As for us, it is enough for us to reform ourselves and to reform those below us in responsibility!

Loyalty to Allah means regarding Allah the Exalted as a supreme, sacred value for which one gets angry .. Fine, what if you committed sins and offenses and felt nothing? This means you do not regard Allah the Exalted as a supreme value for which one gets angry! This means you do not understand the meaning of (Allah) and do not understand Allah's right over you! And Allah's right over you is that you be angry at yourself for His sake, not angry at Him for your own sake!

Some people go through crises and say: we are angry at Allah! Because they are ignorant of Allah the Exalted, of the religion, of Islam, of legislation, and of decree and destiny! If there are in the world those who got angry at Allah the Exalted because of their ignorance, then why do the others, those sound in understanding, mind and soul, not embrace the thought of anger for Allah the Exalted?!

The greatest meanings of anger for Allah the Exalted on earth are the meanings of not wronging people, because wronging people is an assault on Allah's creatures, which means a direct assault on Allah's commands .. So Allah the Exalted made people's rights on the Day of Resurrection belong to the people as the basis of the judgment on them, a punishment for whoever assaults Allah's creatures: He makes him humiliated before the holder of the right on the Day of Resurrection, begging him and pleading with him to pardon him!

And among the signs of anger for Allah the Exalted is that, if you intend a great sin, you say: Allah the Exalted commanded that it not be done, and I am loyal to Allah, and loyalty to Allah means that I am angry for Him. So how am I angry for Him .. I am angry for Him at my own soul, which deals ill-manneredly with His law and what He commanded .. That you feel anger at yourself for Allah's sake .. that you feel loathing for yourself when it commands you to evil, for Allah's sake .. means that you have come to love Allah more than yourself .. And when you are loyal to Allah the Exalted, you certainly come to love Allah the Exalted before yourself .. And here piety becomes impossible, and your commitment impossible to come about, except through love of Allah the Exalted .. That is because those who are pious out of fear of the Fire will stumble a lot .. and will err a lot .. These have never been loyal to Allah the Exalted .. and have not loved Him … These are cowards who only fear the Fire .. And what a difference between a fearful one trembling at the Fire""")

t(16, 150, """meaning he worships Allah the Exalted with a worship of self-interest .. keeps to morals with a commitment of self-interest .. his relationship with Allah is a relationship of self-interest .. O Lord, I will fear You, just do not put me into the Fire .. This is a relationship of self-interest with no love for Allah in it .. and one who obeys Allah out of love for Allah .. who does good to people out of love for Allah, not because he fears people's rights on the Day of Resurrection! It is a difference like the distance between the seventh heaven and the seventh earth: between a person who does good on earth because he wants Paradise and its bliss and wants salvation from the Fire, and a person who does good because he loves Allah .. because he truly loves Allah .. because he truly feels Allah in his heart .. Allah, truly: when he hears His name his heart dances .. quivers .. every kind of beautiful feeling floods him .. he loves the Lord .. And can the Lord not be loved? Can our Lord not be loved, without whom we would not have come into this life to know Him? It is enough that He, sanctified be His names, gave us the chance to be born and not die stillborn, so that we may know Him. Did the miscarried newborn, when it came down miscarried from its mother's womb, know Him as we knew Him, we who were enabled to live and so came to know Allah the Exalted?

Is there a loyalty to Allah that could truly be logical, deserved and obligatory upon us to live, after He gave us all that He gave us! How, after knowing our Mighty Lord, do we worship Him for a Paradise and a Fire? Worship in the manner of Paradise and Fire will not produce in you loyalty to Allah. It will never produce it. You will live and die without having been loyal to Allah! What loss is greater .. and what catastrophe is bigger? That you live and die without having tasted loyalty, because you have not tasted love of Allah in your heart. And everyone who lives for a Paradise and a Fire and says I love Allah is a liar: either deceived, fooled by his own soul and by Satan, or he does not truly feel love of Allah in his heart but claims it and lies to himself and to people!

If you know who Allah is with correct knowledge, you will love Him .. and if you love Him you will be loyal to Him .. and if you are loyal to Him, evil deeds, small and great, will become rejected in your sight, except for tiny slips not seen under a microscope, every now and then! If you are loyal to Allah the Exalted, commitment and discipline will become very easy for you, like a drink of water .. And those who have strayed, wandered and been lost will say of you: he claims to be righteous! Because they do not understand how a person can actually be righteous at 99% or 99.9%. They do not understand. Because for them to understand and believe that the earth truly has righteous men and women at these levels, they must read this whole article of mine; and the problem is not in merely reading it, the problem is whether they will understand it at all or not. As for the righteous men and women among the readers, men and women of hearts and insight, they will understand every letter of this article, and it may, if Allah the Exalted wills, change everything in their lives for them.""")

t(16, 1310, """When opposites met, the whole truth became known! This one says to that one, you are a sinner; another says to another, you are a disbeliever; a third says to a third, you are misguided; and a fourth says to another, you follow unsound talk that contradicts the Book and the Sunnah .. The opposites met in the age of the internet .. openly, plainly, in broad daylight .. So truths were uncovered, myths fell, and myths were confirmed and became truths; the path of the believers became clear, and the Ummah came to know what was a lie and what was true! The upshot is that the result that will prevail is reverence for the Companions and reverence for the Prophet's Household, complete silence about history, and correction of the tampering that came in the texts other than the Book of Allah the Exalted, which people pass around as manifest truth. But this is not the place to present all these thorny issues, because they are in the hundreds, not the dozens. And the day all those chronic files are closed is a day on which the Ummah will not be allowed, on Friday pulpits or other pulpits, the Ummah will not be allowed to busy itself with any of this. And this is not my talk; rather, this is how the ABCs of any rightly guided rule speak.""")

t(16, 1865, """Constricting Muslim society by cutting off all lawful means of recreation in this society is a betrayal of the trust of the human being .. the human who was told in the Book of our Mighty Lord that he was created to worship Allah the Exalted, and was also told much about preserving himself and not destroying himself, about travelling the earth and building it up, and much in clear verses that make the right life a life of balance between the share of the Hereafter and the permissible share of this world allowed by the Book and the Sunnah.""")

t(17, 575, """Independence is life .. Independence does not mean that we live in a cave .. Independence is that you live as people live .. marry .. have children .. have around you those whom Allah the Exalted brings near to you, people who live alongside you in the same life .. But you do not live among them accepting an injustice, or applauding a transgression, or siding with an oppressor, or coexisting with harm.
Open the pictures so the meaning becomes clear""")

t(17, 1765, """He will not be guided .. will not be guided .. will not be guided .. he who worships his own self, deafens his ears to the truth and refuses to admit what his own self commits .. He will not be guided until the camel passes through the eye of the needle""")

t(18, 420, """Press and rotate""")

t(18, 1470, """Paradise is an honor and a distinction .. and the earth is a long human queue; had we grasped its reality, we would all stand in the queue politely, with no telling who stands at the front from who stands at the back, because it is not a queue of distinction or honoring, but a queue of waiting .. When we stand in a co-op queue to buy a chicken, then when we reach the seller all that happens is that he gives us the chicken and then says: Next! In waiting queues there is neither distinction nor honoring.""")

t(19, 175, """The meeting of cultures is the warmth of humanity .. It is a delight for one place to be a warm embrace for the sons and daughters of Adam whom Iblis tormented and crushed for a hundred years""")

t(19, 1320, """Offering what is beneficial, in every place and in every position in life, is reward and recompense in everyone's scale of deeds""")

t(19, 2410, """A question I answered several months ago was repeated by a brother or sister in the comments yesterday: about the Mahdi's dislike of the pledge of allegiance while he knows himself. The Mahdi's knowledge of himself before his pledge is definite; hundreds of visions over the past years have corroborated it. As for his dislike of the matter, knowing a thing does not prevent dislike: a sick man knows of his illness and is brought a medicine; he may push it back with his hand, not wanting it, or turn his face away from the medicine's bitterness, although the sick man knows he is sick. As for the man's dislike of the matter, it is a momentary dislike and not a general dislike as most people and most speakers understood it. That is because general dislike requires that he believe that Allah's decrees do not come to pass merely because a person dislikes something; then yes, general dislike would become logical, from a man I do not think needs to be taught the ABCs of""")

t(20, 165, """destiny! Whoever believes deep inside that as soon as he dislikes a thing, that thing will not happen, then we would say that the man dislikes this matter with a general dislike and not a momentary one. This means that inwardly he rejects the matter altogether and will strive to push it away from himself, as one strives who pushes a thing away so that it does not happen and does not occur, believing he will actually succeed in that, that the matter will not come about, and that he will escape the fatigue, exhaustion and responsibility. But is this talk even acceptable in religion, jurisprudence, reason and logic? Of course this is empty talk. So knowing a thing with certainty requires that belief in it has occurred, and believing a thing with certain belief requires that the soul grasps all of the truth in full; general dislike in this case becomes acting toward oneself, with the person acting before himself. And if he is pledged allegiance reluctantly when he appears, disliking and refusing with a general dislike, then he is acting before the people, Allah forbid, for he is the righteous man; so how would we describe him with such a thing, unless we ourselves are ignorant of the true correct understanding? The correct understanding is clear: the dislike on the day of his appearance is not a general dislike but a momentary one. Whoever refuses the medicine and turns his face from it takes the medicine in the end, however much he turns his face away and however much he pushes it back with his hand; that is a moment of momentary dislike. But the sick man knows for certain that he is sick, so he knows he is not well, and knows he will take the medicine by decree, because that is the nature of things. Unlike the Imam, whose destiny is stronger than that of the sick man taking the medicine: it remains open to the sick man to refuse the medicine and have his illness worsen, or to recover without medicine; but that man knows his destiny is not open to alteration like the destiny of the sick man who refuses the medicine for a moment. Accordingly, the man refuses the matter with a momentary refusal, and that refusal on that day is a purely human emotional state, understandable, conceivable and very logical for a person who finds the matter very heavy; and it truly is, as we all understand, very heavy. So the mistaken notions must be corrected, because unfortunately all who spoke on end-times issues over the last 20 years concurred that his dislike is a general dislike. This is a plain contradiction of reason and logic, an understanding that does not hold up before the facts of reason and logic and, before them, the understanding of destiny. Their explanations to people were unfortunately undisciplined and shallow, and people repeated the saying about dislike after them without understanding, except for men and women known only to Allah who understood it within themselves! O Allah, yes; and Allah knows best, the Ummah will never lack men and women of understanding in it.""")

t(20, 1215, """Al-Jifri: My master al-Rifa'i (his master, that is): the Prophet brought out his hand to him and he kissed it, with the people as witnesses!""")

t(20, 1425, """In the saying of Allah, our Mighty Lord, sanctified be His names: {Or like the one who passed by a town fallen in upon its roofs. He said: "How will Allah bring this to life after its death?" So Allah caused him to die for a hundred years, then raised him. He said: "How long have you remained?" He said: "I have remained a day or part of a day." He said: "Rather, you have remained a hundred years. Look at your food and your drink: they have not spoiled. And look at your donkey; and that We may make you a sign for the people. And look at the bones, how We raise them, then clothe them with flesh." When it became clear to him, he said: "I know that Allah has power over all things."}

The donkey died and its bones remained and did not decay into dust in 100 years .. but the food was as it was .. Bacteria did not touch it for a hundred years!

The power of Allah the Exalted has nothing to do with physics""")

t(20, 1955, """Global cities and the imbalance of the foreign population structure""")

t(21, 575, """They say with their mouths: "at Allah's door" of the destitute poor man! And they do not fear an overwhelming calamity descending and striking them! Is Allah's door to be attached to poverty and begging? Is illness, poverty and need to be attached to Allah's door? When one stands at Allah's door, even without its being opened, the whole world opens up! So how is it when it opens? I know these are words not meant by most people, but only my fear for those who say them makes me address frightening words to them, because the matter, before the majesty of Allah our Mighty Lord, is frightening for one who does not reflect on what he utters before uttering it.

"At Allah's door" is said, among those for all of whom we fear Allah's punishment, of every destitute, poor, homeless person, so it inevitably becomes, without argument or dispute, a link between the door of Allah the Exalted and standing at it on one side, and poverty, failure and ruin on the other. So let these brothers and sisters fear Allah the Exalted, and not make the door of Aramco, the door of Facebook, the door of the big local companies and the door of the big global companies a door of success, honor and good, and Allah's door a door of failure, ruin and poverty, thereby exalting the doors of companies, the doors of institutions and the doors of employers, despising Allah's door, describing Allah's door with what is not truly in it, and so behaving ill-manneredly with their Lord!

As for the poor, the destitute, and the one who met failure in life as a trial and a test for him, he is at Allah's door hoping for His mercy and His granting of success, and is not at Allah's door as an outcome, as though he ended up at Allah's door because of failure and ruin, as a result. That would mean that those at the door of Aramco, Facebook and iPhone, and all who work in global companies, have no need of Allah's door. The comparison is clear and the meaning is clear: whoever wants the advice will take it in, and whoever refuses, let him leave it .. As for us here, we have all discharged our responsibility""")

t(21, 1440, """Can justice produce a Qarun-like Ummah?
It is reported in the authentic hadith that the distribution of wealth by handfuls, without counting, continues for seven, eight or 9 years, which is something everyone knows. A note that must be published on this issue. Can justice, if applied incorrectly, be a cause of corruption on earth?

Justice can produce the right model and fulfil Islam's aim for the human being if it is founded on a correct method, sound rules and wise governance. The opposite of that: without rules, controls and wise, governing laws, granting people wealth without laws becomes a great harm to them; they will deviate and do as they please .. They will not work .. they will not study .. they will not go to the mosques, nor will they pray .. Their souls will tyrannize one another, and they will turn into Qarun-like men and Qarun-like women because of the great volume of gold currency in their homes and in their hands. Here justice becomes something that brings about corruption on earth and not its reform, because it was applied without setting regulating laws that protect the human from himself, protect society from its individuals, and ensure a move to the better and not to the worse through the distribution of that wealth.""")

t(21, 2120, """Why did the man say of himself that he was the greediest of Muhammad's Ummah?!
A hasan hadith
From Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: "I give you glad tidings of the Mahdi. He is sent at a time of discord among people and of earthquakes, and he fills the earth with equity and justice as it was filled with tyranny and injustice. The dweller of the heaven and the dweller of the earth are pleased with him. He divides wealth sihahan." A man said to him: "What is sihahan?" He said: "Equally among the people. And Allah fills the hearts of the Ummah of Muhammad ﷺ with contentment, and his justice encompasses them, until he orders a caller, who calls out: 'Who has a need for wealth?' And none of the people stands except one man, who says: 'I.' He says: 'Go to the keeper', meaning the treasurer, 'and say to him: the Mahdi orders you to give me wealth.' He says to him: 'Scoop.' Then, when he has put it in his lap and bundled it up, he regrets and says: 'I was the greediest of the Ummah of Muhammad ﷺ; or was what sufficed them not enough for me?'" He said: "So he returns it, but it is not accepted from him, and he is told: 'We do not take back a thing we have given.' And so it is for seven years, or eight years, or nine years; then there is no good in living after him", or he said: "then there is no good in life after him." I say: al-Tirmidhi and others narrated it in a much abridged form.

Ahmad narrated it with several chains, and Abu Ya'la in a much abridged form, and the narrators of both are trustworthy""")

t(22, 170, """What appears from this hadith, and Allah knows best, is that the filling of the Ummah's hearts with contentment before the Great Battle and during the 9 years is not connected with the whole Ummah having been guided and become entirely pious and pure, because a third of the army of the Great Battle flees. As for the filling of people's hearts with contentment in the 9 years before the Great Battle, its outcome and cause are explained by another authentic hadith, in which it came that the handing out of gold to people continues for 9 years, meaning that people will obtain gold for 9 years; this is an explicit and clear text in a hadith of authentic chain. The upshot, then, is that Muslims will obtain wealth, houses, farms, fruits and life, and will lack nothing, and not a single problem will remain in the life of any of them. Then, when all their problems fall away, they will submit to a social system in which all forms of corruption are shut out; they will find themselves in a new social climate, will submit to new social controls, and will grow up anew, even the adults among them. For people's moving to hearts filled with contentment means their turning away from the world being the ruler and master in their hearts! This means that most of what will happen to them, and Allah knows best, is that they will submit to a new way of life in which they are pushed to understand their religion correctly, to understand the reality of this world and the Hereafter fully, and to realize that death is not far from anyone, and that these years of ease which the Prophet ﷺ foretold, he foretold not for corruption on earth but for joy to enter hearts, to live a tremendous life for 9 years, and then to proceed to Allah the Exalted for the Day of Resurrection.

As for the one who said of himself: I was the greediest of Muhammad's Ummah, this is not because Muhammad's Ummah on that day is poor and the man wants wealth because he is poor. Had he been poor, he would not have been greedy. Had he been poor, he would have deserved the wealth. Had he been poor, he would not have blamed himself. The point is that he is not poor and not in need, and so here greed occurred .. and he returned it only because he does not need it at all .. That is why no one else went to the treasury .. Is it because people are poor that they do not need wealth, while the treasury is full of tons of gold? The answer, I believe, has now become clear .. No one is in need of wealth .. Everyone is in their homes, farms and fruits, and their homes are already full of wealth; they lack no wealth, this man included.""")

t(22, 1115, """That the wealth truly be wealth that the earth brings out as gold and silver and every kind of provision .. then yes .. wealth is handed out by handfuls even to millions of Muslims .. and then people will serve the Ummah in government work for the sake of Allah .. and in the markets non-Muslim newcomers, seeking their livelihoods, will work ..

Some brothers ask about the coming picture of the future .. having read the hadiths of authentic chain about wealth being handed out to people by handfuls .. But as a personal judgment I say: the handing out of wealth that the hadiths establish definitively, those same hadiths establish the existence of large numbers of Muslims, which makes handing out wealth to hundreds of millions difficult, merely on looking at the nature of people's circulation of money across their different ages. So it appears, and Allah knows best, that the handing out of wealth to all these millions happens because the earth brings out all its treasures in that era, so that wealth is like mountains, without exaggeration or fable .. Handing out wealth to people, as we say in colloquial speech (by the sack), means something that never happened before in human history; and since the noble hadith established it, it is established, and no one has any way to deny it.

The pictures show the phase of the 9 years in Jerusalem, Allah willing, and the pictures of Jerusalem are a model of a wealthy Ummah in every land inhabited by Muslims, not Jerusalem alone. According to reason and logic, as the explanation here will show, it is a natural phase and life in it is natural; during it the Dajjal will not have emerged, and the Ummah of Islam will be at the peak of its strength on earth .. So when we understand this handing out of wealth to Muslims, it will mean several basic matters:
1- Muslims working in government departments will work out of love of serving their Ummah, not in pursuit of livelihood.
2- Professions, crafts and trades such as restaurants and shops, and all that relates to the private market, will, on this view, be active in the hands of Muslims partnering in trade with non-Muslims, because the incentive for trade, effort and toil will not exist among Muslims.
3- Motivating Muslims to work and learn, under a state with this kind of wealth, will not be because they need to develop themselves in order to seek livelihood after self-development; rather, it seems we are before a new historic human-social equation and a phenomenon unique in human history that has not happened before, such that incentives turn into duties subject to new rules of social work, far from the traditional thinking based on a person's need for money through a job, so that he is forced to learn and exert effort.
4- The hadith of the handing out of wealth means the establishment, for 9 years, of a global state whose geographic area is unprecedented, in which Muslims have the first historic opportunity in their history to devote themselves to worship in a better way (bearing in mind that no person prays 24 hours), as the abundance of wealth lifts from them dozens of kinds of responsibilities of toil, fatigue and effort, so that the available free time becomes very great. This is something new at the level of worship in the Ummah, such that there was no such state in its past history. And this means the rise of a society in need of a new organization of life and of setting new, unprecedented rules, controls and foundations, the like of which has not been applied before in history, so that the handing out of wealth does not turn into a gateway to corruption on earth. For the hadith spoke of wealth being handed out by handfuls, but it did not speak of the laws that will be set to protect the Muslim from the trial of wealth, lest he take wealth without count and then sleep, without worship, without knowledge, and without improving the quality of his character and abilities. The handing out is established by the text of the hadith, but the controls are left unmentioned in the hadith.
5- Some err when they think that Muslims, when wealth is handed out to them, do not need life; yet life has markets, food, mosques, acts of worship and gifts at the festivals, and life has hundreds of human details that cannot stop when a person obtains much wealth. So people think that a Muslim's obtaining much wealth means his going into his house and worshipping around the clock, 24 hours. Did these think that Islam is given victory as a creed and a thought at the end of time in order to produce an Ummah asleep inside the house? These understood the handing out of wealth in a way that clashes with the nature of human life and, more importantly, clashes with Islam's message for the human being, and they thought that the handing out of wealth means people worshipping 24 hours. Then who will sow, harvest, sell, manufacture and build? So the handing out of wealth never means that life stops, but""")

t(23, 155, """the handing out of wealth will impose social challenges that will require laws, and will impose many non-social challenges too that will require regulating laws, so that the Ummah is not lost. Our Prophet ﷺ foretold justice and foretold wealth being handed out by handfuls and that it will not be counted, but he also spoke of an era whose title is guidance and right conduct .. And guidance, right conduct and rightly guided action are a complete system of work that knows what it is doing, and realizes that justice itself can sometimes, if applied incorrectly, be a cause of the corruption of the earth!""")

t(23, 1445, """Our children today are scattered across the earth .. dispersed .. no homeland .. no belonging .. no safety or warmth .. But .. tomorrow, by the power of our Mighty Lord, they will live their youth, their adolescence and their childhood here .. in these streets""")

t(24, 1135, """Muslims too are human beings, O you who want them to go on meeting among ruins and on the corners of stinking, filthy alleys so that you can convince yourselves that this is Islam; and when you are objected to, you say Islam is a religion of asceticism, and you have lied, for Islam is a religion of balance! Islam is innocent of your deviant thought .. This is the thought of circling around dry tree leaves and the droppings of beasts, of sitting in caves on mountaintops because so-and-so has been sleeping there for 1000 years, and of rolling in the dust .. and of regarding the alleged, false asceticism that is performed as an act today, regarding it as an obligation on every Muslim!""")

t(24, 2390, """After long years of the human being deprived of privacy and its beauty .. Re-grounding values, ideals and morals in public gathering places that serve men and women, such as famous and distinguished restaurants .. Our societies need the tools for protecting the privacy of husbands, wives and women in general to be reactivated""")
